---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ArrowLeft } from '@lucide/astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy - Daan Rosendal" description="What the chat with Junior saves and how to have it deleted.">
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-12 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
    <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 hover:text-gray-900 dark:hover:text-white transition-colors">
      <ArrowLeft size={14} />
      Home
    </a>
  </nav>

  <article class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
    <h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Privacy</h1>
    <p>Chats with Junior are saved, so I can see how people use him.</p>
    <p><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Saved:</strong> your questions, his answers, the time, the page you were on, your country, and basic visit details such as device type, browser, and language.</p>
    <p><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Kept for 90 days:</strong> your city and a code made from your IP address that cannot be turned back into it.</p>
    <p><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Never saved:</strong> your IP address, or any cookie or tracking ID.</p>
    <p>Stored at Cloudflare in the EU until I delete it. Removed data can stay in backups for up to 7 days. To have a chat deleted, email <a href="mailto:contact@daanrosendal.com" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-gray-900 dark:hover:text-white">contact@daanrosendal.com</a>.</p>
    <p>If you move or resize the minimised chat window, its position and size stay in your own browser and are never sent to me.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
